Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 04:30:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: record the SPK as not carried, a GMAT
 time-representation finding

The gmat job's sixth run (Flight dynamics run 42560008632, at 8941ea41e) read the SPK out in GMAT's
ICRF axes: the rotation is gone (fitted 0.000 mas), the worst node is 1.19 mm and 3.0e-10 km/s from
the written state, all of it along the velocity (implied dt -1.91 to +0.72 us per node, within
0.44 us of the reported epoch offsets, about one ulp of an A.1 MJD; at most 2.3e-10 km across the
velocity). GMAT returns the kernel's state at the epochs it can represent, which its 16-digit
report cannot print exactly. The seat did not amend the rule after this result, so the SPK row is
not carried.

RESULTS (C7): the status, the GMAT rows (SPK not carried, OEM refused), findings 4 and 5 (the
representable epochs; GMAT's MJ2000Eq axes 44.4 mas from its ICRF axes), the sixth run and future
work (a full-precision readout). The flight-dynamics README gains GMAT's results; the workflow
comment says the gmat job is red by design.
